--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
InboxPage.tsx is the top-level notifications inbox scoped to the active (non-
archived) items. It calls useVehicles() + useAlertRules(), renders a
PageContainer (title "Inbox", subtitle, copyLink, "View archived" action linking
to /notifications/archived) and reuses <InboxBody archived={false} vehicles rules />
so the bulk-action set offers Archive (not Restore) and the grouped/flat toggle is
available. The web InboxBody owns the notification-log feeds (useNotificationLogs /
useNotificationGroups) + the inbox mutations, auto-marks-read on open (markOnOpen),
exposes the empty-state CTA "Configure alert rules" -> /notifications/studio, and
builds ruleMap (rule.id->rule) + vehicleMap (vehicle.id->vehicle) from the two
props to label rows and decide drill-through (rule = ruleMap[log.alert_id];
vehicle = vehicleMap[rule.vehicle_id]).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The shared A3 InboxBody feature-view already exists
(io.teslasync.android.featureviews.inboxbody.InboxBody) and owns every inbox data
state (loading skeleton / hard-error+retry / inbox empty / content / stale-offline)
for its flat + grouped feeds, the bulk toolbar, the per-row context menu, the
select-all tri-state, and the delete confirmation. This page is its active host: it
binds the feeds (archived=false), joins rows with the page's two web hooks, renders
the PageContainer-equivalent header, enables markOnOpen, and wires the mutations +
the empty-state CTA. The row-join (ruleMap/vehicleMap) is the SAME framework-free
logic the sibling ArchivedPage authored (the web shares it inside InboxBody.tsx for
both routes), so it is reused via import rather than duplicated (DRY) — no
out-of-scope edit to ArchivedPage.

New files (package io.teslasync.android.notifications.inbox):
  - InboxPageModel.kt      Registration(ROUTE_ID notificationsInbox, WEB_PATH
                           /notifications/inbox, ARCHIVED_PATH /notifications/archived,
                           STUDIO_PATH /notifications/studio, SLUG InboxPage,
                           archivedDeepLink/studioDeepLink), INBOX_FILTERS
                           (archived=false), recordInboxPageOpened. Reuses
                           toInboxNotifications/toInboxGroups/mapData from the sibling
                           …notifications.archived package (DRY).
  - InboxPageSource.kt     InboxPageSource seam + inboxPageSourceOf(repo,
                           vehiclesStore): active notificationLogs/groups, alertRules,
                           vehicles + the 6 inbox mutations.
  - InboxPageViewModel.kt  BaseFeedViewModel; flatState/groupState as
                           StateFlow<UiState<…>> via refreshTrigger ▸ flatMapLatest ▸
                           combine(logs, alertRules, vehicles) ▸ mapData ▸ asUiState;
                           refresh/retry; the 7 mutation callbacks (each refreshes the
                           family on success); recordViewOpened.
  - InboxPageIcons.kt      InboxPageGlyphs.Archive — a 24×24 stroked vector (web lucide
                           Archive) for the "View archived" action leading icon, since
                           TeslaGlyphs ships none (mirrors GlancePageIcons precedent).
  - InboxPage.kt           Stateful entry (viewModel factory) + stateful overload
                           (collectAsStateWithLifecycle, DeepLinkRouter seams for
                           "View archived" + the studio CTA, InboxPageActions) +
                           stateless InboxPageContent (header + InboxBody archived=false,
                           markOnOpen=true, onConfigureRules) + InboxPageHeader
                           (PageTitle + subtitle + copy-link IconButton + View-archived
                           Button with the Archive glyph).
  - InboxPageHost.kt       InboxRoute() binds HttpNotificationsRepository (shared
                           resilient client + offline cache) + the shared S8
                           VehiclesStore; InboxPageHost.register() ->
                           PageHosts.register("notificationsInbox").

Edits (registration + string catalog + ledger only):
  - TeslaSyncApplication.kt   import + InboxPageHost.register() at process start.
  - res/values/strings.xml    3 keys (translation_notifications_inbox_{title,subtitle,
                              viewArchived}); copy-link reuses the existing
                              translation_common_copyLink_action.
  - apps/parity/android-ledger.json  page:notifications/Inbox row (done, 4/4).

Notes:
  - SI: no notification field is unit-bearing (ids, ISO timestamps, free text, a
    severity enum) — no SI conversion; date/locale formatting is at the render
    boundary inside InboxBody (S5).
  - States: InboxBody renders loading / empty(inbox) / error+retry / content /
    stale-offline for the bound feeds (verified by the shared InboxBodyUiTest).
  - i18n: every visible literal via stringResource (ADR-014); web key names kept.
  - a11y: PageTitle heading, copy-link IconButton contentDescription, Button label;
    InboxBody supplies row/select/archive/freshness content descriptions (ADR-015).
  - Nav: "View archived" + the empty-state "Configure alert rules" CTA route through
    the DeepLinkRouter — the sanctioned page-host seam (no LocalNavController is
    exposed to hosts), the same bridge AppScaffold.NotificationDeepLinkHandler feeds
    into Navigation-Compose; callbacks are hoisted so the surface stays unit-testable.

